description:
A single OpenSearch analysis component: a tokenizer, a char filter, or a token filter. Two shapes:

  // Built-in component — just the OpenSearch name:
  { "name": "standard" }
  { "name": "lowercase" }
  { "name": "html_strip" }

  // Custom component — any unique name + an OpenSearch JSON definition under 'definition':
  { "name": "my_edge_ngram",
    "definition": "{\"type\":\"edge_ngram\",\"min_gram\":2,\"max_gram\":20}" }
  { "name": "my_stop",
    "definition": "{\"type\":\"stop\",\"stopwords\":[\"the\",\"a\",\"of\"]}" }

For the full inventory of types and parameters see the OpenSearch docs for <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/tokenizers/index/'>tokenizers</a>, <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/character-filters/index/'>char filters</a>, and <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/token-filters/index/'>token filters</a>. At index-build time custom-component names are namespaced by their owning TextAnalyzer's qualified name so multiple analyzers can reuse the same local name without collision.
